tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/attendance-vs-labor-data.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Attendance vs. Labor Data: The Difference Between Knowing When Someone Worked and What They Worked On</h3><p>A punch can tell you when an employee worked. Labor data explains what those hours mean—job, department, project, cost center, worktag or activity.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/labor-codes-worktags-edge.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Job Codes, Cost Centers &amp; Worktags at the Clock: Capture Labor Detail Without Slowing Employees Down</h3><p>Workday can represent a sophisticated labor and costing model. The employee should not have to navigate that complexity at the clock.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/department-transfer-split-punch.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Department Transfers &amp; Split Punches: Capture Labor Moves Without Creating Payroll Cleanup</h3><p>Employees change jobs, departments and activities during the day.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/rounding-rules-timekeeping.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Time Rounding: Where Policy, Workday Configuration and the Clock Must Align</h3><p>Rounding is not a time-clock feature to switch on casually.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/duplicate-punch-prevention.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Duplicate Punches: Prevent the Error at the Source Before It Becomes Payroll Cleanup</h3><p>A second tap can create a second transaction, a confusing timecard and unnecessary manager work.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/employee-self-service-clock.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Employee Self-Service at the Time Clock: Turn a Punch Point Into a Useful Workforce Touchpoint</h3><p>A shared time clock can do more than capture IN and OUT—but it should not become a crowded HR portal.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Time &amp; Labor Data" href="insights/shift-types-workforce-design.html"><div class="cat">Time &amp; Labor Data</div><h3>Shift Types &amp; Time Collection: Design for the Way Your Workforce Actually Works</h3><p>Day shifts are easy to model.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/intelligent-enforcement-point.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>The Time Clock Is Becoming an Intelligent Enforcement Point</h3><p>The best workforce controls resolve avoidable errors while the employee is still present.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/employee-attestation-strategy.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Employee Attestation: Use It to Capture Context, Not to Replace Policy</h3><p>An attestation is useful only when the answer supports a real decision.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/meal-rest-break-controls.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Meal and Rest Break Controls: Prevention, Attestation and Exception Handling</h3><p>Meal and rest-break workflows should implement approved policy, preserve accurate records and handle legitimate exceptions.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/schedule-lockout-design.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Schedule Lockouts: Controlling Unauthorized Time Without Blocking Legitimate Work</h3><p>Schedule controls can reduce unauthorized early and late punches, but only when schedule data is timely and legitimate work is not blocked.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/certificate-lockout-safety.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Certification-Based Punch Controls: Connecting Workforce Eligibility to the Employee Interaction</h3><p>Eligibility controls can connect certifications, training or other approved status to the workforce interaction.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/biometric-consent-workforce.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Biometric Consent at the Workforce Edge: Technology Must Follow the Organization’s Privacy Program</h3><p>Biometric timekeeping is an identity-lifecycle and privacy program—not just an authentication feature.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/auditability-workforce-data.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Auditability in Workforce Data Collection: What Should You Be Able to Explain Later?</h3><p>When a workforce event is questioned months later, can you reconstruct what happened?</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Controls &amp; Compliance" href="insights/manager-override-controls.html"><div class="cat">Controls &amp; Compliance</div><h3>Manager Overrides Without Losing Control: Designing the Exception to the Rule</h3><p>Real operations need exceptions.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Enterprise Time Clocks" href="insights/time-clock-buyers-guide.html"><div class="cat">Enterprise Time Clocks</div><h3>The Enterprise Time Clock Buyer’s Guide: 12 Questions to Ask Before You Standardize</h3><p>Twelve questions that help enterprise buyers evaluate employee experience, identity, environment, integration, fleet operations, lifecycle and the company behind the clock.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Enterprise Time Clocks" href="insights/purpose-built-vs-tablet.html"><div class="cat">Enterprise Time Clocks</div><h3>Purpose-Built Time Clock or Tablet? Compare the Real Enterprise Cost and Lifecycle</h3><p>A tablet may look inexpensive until enclosure, mounting, power, authentication, management, replacement and lifecycle are included.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="card tw-flex tw-min-h-[270px] tw-flex-col tw-rounded-[16px] tw-border tw-border-[var(--line)] tw-bg-white tw-p-[24px] tw-shadow-[0_10px_28px_rgba(20,27,70,.06)] tw-transition-[transform,box-shadow] tw-duration-[180ms] hover:tw-translate-y-[-3px] hover:tw-shadow-[var(--shadow)]" data-cat="Enterprise Time Clocks" href="insights/rugged-time-clocks.html"><div class="cat">Enterprise Time Clocks</div><h3>Rugged or Standard? Match Time-Clock Design to the Environment</h3><p>Standardize the platform, then match the physical endpoint to the environment.</p><div class="read">Read insight <span>→</span></div></a><a class="